# Migration scratch space.
#
# `.tmp/` holds one-off probes, extracted old-file snapshots and run artifacts (including
# SQLite files). They were never meant to be tracked: a git worktree added here shows up as
# an embedded repository, and the sqlite/wal files change on every run. The release snapshots
# that *were* tracked (`.tmp/deploy/**`, `.tmp/update/**`) are removed in the same commit -
# they are v1.6.x vendor copies, not sources, and `pack.sh` only reads them if they exist.
/.tmp/
